    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2921B\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to gender\nbalance in state and local public authorities; and providing for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide gender balance in the appointment of members to appointed\npositions of state and local public authorities, industrial development\nagencies and local development corporations.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the public authorities law by adding a new section 2829\nto provide that all appointments to appointive state and local public\nauthorities shall be gender balanced, to the extent practicable.\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York is behind when compared nationally and globally on correcting\nthe leadership gap between women and men. Although women make up more\nthan half of New York's population, they make up an underwhelming 22% of\npositions on state boards.\n\nTo address the gender gap in New York, this bill would require appoint-\ning powers to ensure public authorities, industrial development agen-\ncies, and local development corporations are gender balanced by appoint-\ning an equal number of women and men to serve, to the extent practica-\nble. The bill also provides measures appointing powers would be able to\nfollow in the event boardmake-up cannot be comprised of 50% women and\n50% men.\n\nWhile legislation addressing women on boards and women in the workforce\nis more common outside of the United States, it is imperative that we\nuse these successful models to effectively increase the diversity of\nboards across the state.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023: Passed Assembly; 3rd Reading Senate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON TILE STATE:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect August 1, 2024 and shall expire on August 1,\n2034.\n",
